## Origin

phpcpd-next began as a fork of PHP Copy/Paste Detector (PHPCPD),
Copyright (c) 2011-2023 Sebastian Bergmann, which was licensed under the
BSD 3-Clause License.

No file in `src/` carries that attribution any longer: every inherited file has
been rewritten from its specification, each one proved to produce byte-identical
output before its header was changed. `php bench/check-provenance.php` measures
this and reports the inventory at zero. The relicensing above is that inventory
reaching zero, not a decision taken in spite of it.

No BSD 3-Clause text is shipped, because no code under it is. The closest
thing to an exception is acknowledged rather than licensed: the membership of
the ignored-token set in `src/Detector/Strategy/AbstractStrategy.php` — which
nine of PHP's token types carry no program — came from the original, and is a
fact about the language rather than a way of writing one. A licence file
covering nothing would assert an encumbrance this package does not carry.

That the tool exists at all is owed to the original. The idea, the problem, and
fourteen years of it being worth solving are Sebastian Bergmann's.
